# Deferred, links

- Dashed Editor chips have no accessible description. Chat chips carry
  `aria-description` in the follow's own words ("No document at that
  address"). In the Editor the state lives on the
  decoration spans (`link-resolution-decorations.ts`) inside the link mark's
  `<a>`, and a description on a generic span is not announced, so a screen
  reader hears an ordinary link until it is followed. Carry the description on
  the `<a>` (for example a link mark view reading the surface's resolution),
  still adding nothing to the schema, the shared document, or the clipboard.
- Pasting into the chat composer leaves `[[…]]` as text. If writers paste
  Obsidian notes into chat, give the composer a paste catalog and mount
  `WikilinkPasteExtension` there, spelling full URIs as chat links do
  (`components/app/composer/`, `links/WikilinkPasteExtension.ts`).
- Unfiled and Uploads documents are not candidates for a pasted `[[Name]]`
  (`pasteTargets` in `features/editor/EditorView.tsx`). Decide whether an
  Unfiled draft or an uploaded file should be linkable by name, and widen the
  filter there if so.
- `[[Name#Heading]]` pastes labeled `Name`; Obsidian shows `Name > Heading`.
  Match Obsidian's label for heading and block links if writers expect it
  (`scanWikilinks` in `links/wikilink-paste.ts`).
- A pasted link keeps Obsidian's heading suffix as written (`Kael.md#The
  Duel`). Unverified: whether following it scrolls to the heading named by
  that text rather than a slug. Check, and make it do so if not
  (`features/links/`, the follow and open path).
